  "comments": "P vs PI vs PID on the same lightly damped plant 1/(s^2+0.5s+1), step at t=1 s. P (Kp=2) oscillates toward 2/3 and keeps a steady-state error; PI (Kp=2, Ki=1) removes the error but overshoots by about 40% and is still ringing at 10 s; PID (Kp=3, Ki=1.5, Kd=1.2) settles at 1 with about 15% overshoot. The first scope overlays the plant outputs, the second the control signals (note the derivative kick at the step).",
  "name": "PID Demo - P vs PI vs PID",
